    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέᾰτο</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seemed,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀεικέλιος δέατ᾽ εἶναι</span>
			<i>methought</i> he was a pitiful fellow, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.242
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰκ ἂν δέατοι,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢν δοκῇ, ὅσᾳ ἂν
				δ.</span>
			, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσῃ ἂν δοκῇ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).6.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Tegea</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπόθ᾽ ἂν δεάσητοι ἀμφοτέροις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				343.24
			</span></i> (Orchom. <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i>); cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέαται: δοκεῖ, δεάμην:
				ἐδοκίμαζον, ἐδόξαζον, δέασθεν</span> (prob.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδόκουν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Root <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεψᾰ</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆλος, δοάσσατο,</span> Skt.
				<i>d[imacracute]deti</i> 'appear'.)</div>
